---
import Footer from '@/components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '@/components/Header.astro';
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PAGE_TITLE } from '@/util/constants';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${PAGE_TITLE}`}
  description="Privacy policy of m1well.com"
  noIndex
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <div class="mw-content">
    <section class="mw-section">
      <div class="mw-container mw-mt-7">
        <div class="mw-section-head">
          <h1 class="mw-section-head-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        </div>

        <div class="mw-alert mw-alert-info m1-legal">
          <div class="mw-alert-content">
            <p class="mw-alert-title">In short</p>
            <p>
              This site sets no cookies, does not track you and has no contact
              form. It is a static site served by GitHub Pages. Besides the page
              itself, your browser makes two requests: one to Unsplash for the
              photo behind the intro, one to my own view counter, which keeps
              nothing but the page and the time. The only thing stored in your
              browser is your light or dark theme choice, and only if you use
              the toggle.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mw-card mw-card-simple mw-prose m1-legal">
          <h2>1. Controller</h2>
          <p>
            The controller responsible for data processing on this website is:
          </p>
          <p>
            Michael Wellner<br />
            Unterboihinger Str. 29<br />
            73240 Wendlingen<br />
            Germany
          </p>
          <p>
            E-mail:{' '}
            <a href="mailto:hallo@formatwerke.de">hallo@formatwerke.de</a>
          </p>

          <h2>2. Hosting on GitHub Pages</h2>
          <p>
            This site is hosted by GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street,
            San Francisco, CA 94107, USA, on its GitHub Pages service. When you
            open a page, GitHub's servers receive what your browser sends with
            every request: your IP address, browser type and version, operating
            system, the page requested, date and time of the request and the
            referring page. GitHub logs the IP address of every visitor for
            security purposes. I have no access to those logs and no influence
            on them. Details are in
            <a
              href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub's privacy statement</a
            >.
          </p>
          <p>
            GitHub, Inc. is certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework,
            so the transfer to the USA rests on the adequacy decision of the
            European Commission (Art. 45 GDPR). The legal basis for hosting the
            site this way is my legitimate interest in a reliably and securely
            delivered website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
          </p>

          <h2>3. The intro photo from Unsplash</h2>
          <p>
            The photo behind the intro section is loaded from
            images.unsplash.com, a service of Unsplash, Inc., Montreal, Canada.
            When your browser fetches it, Unsplash receives your IP address and
            the usual request data. Canada is covered by an adequacy decision of
            the European Commission (Art. 45 GDPR). The legal basis is my
            legitimate interest in a pleasantly designed site (Art. 6(1)(f)
            GDPR). Details are in
            <a
              href="https://unsplash.com/privacy"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">Unsplash's privacy policy</a
            >.
          </p>

          <h2>4. View counter</h2>
          <p>
            On every page view, a small script sends the path of the page to my
            own counter service at custos.m1well.com, which runs on a server in
            Germany. The counter stores only the path and the time of the
            request: no cookie, no identifier, no IP address, no user agent.
            Single views can therefore not be linked to a visit or to a person;
            what remains is a total per page. The legal basis is my legitimate
            interest in knowing which content is read at all (Art. 6(1)(f)
            GDPR).
          </p>

          <h2>5. Cookies, browser storage and embedded content</h2>
          <p>
            This site sets no cookies and does not analyse your behaviour. If
            you use the light/dark toggle in the header, your choice is saved in
            your browser's local storage under the key mw-theme, so the site
            opens in the same theme next time. That value stays on your device
            and is never sent anywhere. Storing it is strictly necessary for the
            function you asked for (Section 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG), so no consent is
            needed and there is no cookie banner.
          </p>
          <p>
            Fonts, icons, stylesheets and scripts are served from this site
            itself. There are no tag managers, no analytics and no social media
            plugins.
          </p>
          <p>
            The links to LinkedIn, Xing, GitHub, daily.dev, dev.to and to the
            projects listed here are ordinary links. Your browser only connects
            to those sites once you click, and their privacy policies apply from
            there.
          </p>

          <h2>6. Contact by e-mail</h2>
          <p>
            If you write me an e-mail, your message and the personal data it
            contains, typically your name, your e-mail address and your request,
            are stored and processed for the purpose of handling it. I do not
            pass this data on without your consent.
          </p>
          <p>
            The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR if your request relates to a
            contract or its initiation. In all other cases it is my legitimate
            interest in handling the requests addressed to me (Art. 6(1)(f)
            GDPR). Your message stays with me until you ask me to delete it or
            the purpose of storing it no longer applies. Statutory retention
            periods remain unaffected.
          </p>

          <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            You have the right to obtain, free of charge, information about the
            personal data I hold about you, its origin, its recipients and the
            purpose of the processing (Art. 15 GDPR), and the right to
            rectification (Art. 16 GDPR) and erasure (Art. 17 GDPR). You can
            demand that processing be restricted (Art. 18 GDPR) and have the
            right to data portability (Art. 20 GDPR). Consent you have given can
            be withdrawn at any time with effect for the future.
          </p>
          <p class="m1-legal-emphasis">
            Right to object: Where your data is processed on the basis of Art.
            6(1)(e) or (f) GDPR, you have the right to object to that processing
            at any time, on grounds relating to your particular situation (Art.
            21 GDPR).
          </p>
          <p>
            You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory
            authority, in particular in the member state of your habitual
            residence, your place of work or the place of the alleged
            infringement. The authority responsible for me is the
            Landesbeauftragte für den Datenschutz und die Informationsfreiheit
            Baden-Württemberg.
          </p>

          <h2>8. Encryption</h2>
          <p>
            This site is delivered over TLS only. You can tell by the https://
            at the start of the address bar and the lock symbol next to it. Data
            you send to me cannot be read by third parties on the way.
          </p>

          <h2>9. Objection to unsolicited advertising</h2>
          <p>
            I object to the use of the contact details published in the legal
            notice for sending advertising or information material that was not
            expressly requested. I reserve the right to take legal action in the
            event of unsolicited advertising, for instance spam e-mails.
          </p>

          <p class="mw-text-sm mw-text-muted mw-mt-8">
            Last updated: September 2026
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
